course: dictionary
lesson: 10305
title: The word tournament
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A tournament is a competition with many games or matches, where players or teams try to win. The clues in a sentence tell you what kind of tournament it is, and whether the word means something from sport or from history.
explain: «At the chess tournament Dev from another school beats Sam on time in the final.» The words chess, final and beats tell you there are many games, the final is the last and most important one, and the winner is the one who wins it.
explain: The same word can be used in a different time. «At tournaments knights jousted, charging at each other on horseback with blunted lances in front of cheering crowds.» Knights, horseback and cheering crowds are the clues: here a tournament was a contest held for sport, long ago.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in. «Maddie missed the girls' football tournament.» If you put in "a competition with many matches", the sentence still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
fact: A tournament is a competition with many games or matches.
fact: Tournaments can be played in sport, such as football, tennis or chess.
fact: In history, a tournament was a contest where knights fought on horseback for sport.
fact: «Win the tournament» means to be the best player or team at the end.
fact: «Knock-out tournament» and «round-robin tournament» are phrases that describe how a tournament is arranged.
exercise: «At the chess tournament Dev from another school beats Sam on time in the final.» What kind of event is a chess tournament? | A shop that sells chess sets | *A competition with many games, where players try to win | A lesson about the history of kings | A day off from school
exercise: «At tournaments knights jousted, charging at each other on horseback.» In this sentence, what was a tournament? | A horse race with no riders | A school trip to a castle | *A contest where knights fought on horseback for sport | A picnic for the whole village
exercise: «Maddie, the best striker, got a detention for fighting and missed the girls' football tournament.» Find and copy the word that shows which sport the tournament was. | best | detention | *football | fighting
test: «Maddie missed the girls' football tournament; she watched from the sidelines as the team lost 2–1.» Which clue shows the team did not win this match? | Watched from the sidelines | Girls' football | *Lost 2–1 | Best striker
test: «At the chess tournament Dev from another school beats Sam on time in the final.» What does the word final suggest? | A game with no winner | A game played at the start | *The last game, which often decides the winner | A game for children only
exam: «Many sports canteens sell mostly chocolate and fizzy drinks, so for a long tournament it is wise to pack sandwiches, fruit and water.» Why does the author say it is wise to pack food and water? | Canteens never open during a tournament | Water is only for the final | *Canteens may sell mostly sweets and fizzy drinks, so you need to bring your own food and water | Fruit is banned at every tournament
